          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I have had reflux for years and now food sometimes sticks going down. How worrying is that, and what does guidance describe about when to investigate?",
          "answer": "If you are experiencing food sometimes sticking while swallowing, it is important to seek medical attention. This could be a sign of a more serious issue, especially if you have had chronic reflux.\n\nAccording to guidance on gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD), \"alarm features\" warrant further investigation. These features include difficulty swallowing, unintended weight loss, or gastrointestinal bleeding. The presence of such symptoms indicates that you should consult a healthcare professional for an evaluation, as they may require medical investigation (source: Gastroenterology society clinical guideline).\n\nWhile chronic reflux can typically be managed with lifestyle modifications and medication, any new or concerning symptoms should be discussed with a clinician. Make sure to share all relevant details about your symptoms during your appointment.\n\nI could not provide specific medical advice on the urgency of your situation, or a detailed overview of treatment options beyond what has been mentioned. If your symptoms are severe or worsening, it is crucial to seek immediate care.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
